OL,3,GNEWSAEx American football pro supports
OL,4,Astroke research
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former professional American football
OL,7,Fplayer who suffered a stroke aged 51 is
OL,8,Fasking for volunteers to take part in
OL,9,Fresearch that could make a "vital
OL,10,Fdifference" to people's lives.
OL,12,FRob Hart, from Edington in Wiltshire,
OL,13,Fwas on the books of several NFL teams
OL,14,Fin America and has continued to keep
OL,15,Ffit since his career ended, running a
OL,16,Fmarathon and completing a 100km (62m)
OL,17,Fcharity run.
OL,19,FBut things took a frightening turn this
OL,20,Fyear when he had a stroke while heading
OL,21,Fto a GP appointment after suffering
OL,22,Fpalpitations.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
